      "id": "future-perfect-continuous",
      "title": "Future Perfect Continuous",
      "icon": "🌀",
      "guide": "## Future Perfect Continuous (Kelasi zamon oldindan davomli ish-harakat)\n\nFuture Perfect Continuous kelajakdagi **ma'lum bir vaqtga qadar davom etib kelayotgan** bo'ladigan ish-harakatning **davomiyligini** ta'kidlash uchun ishlatiladi.\n\n## 1. Shakllanishi (Form)\n• **Tasdiq**: Subject + will have been + V-ing\n  - By next June, I **will have been working** here for five years.\n• **Inkor**: Subject + will not (won't) have been + V-ing\n  - We **won't have been renovating** the house for long by next Friday.\n• **Savol**: Will + Subject + have been + V-ing?\n  - **Will** you **have been learning** English for three years by next week?\n\n*(will barcha shaxs/sonlar uchun bir xil — o'zgarmaydi)*\n\n## 2. Ishlatilishi (Usage)\n1. **Kelajakdagi ma'lum vaqtga qadar davom etadigan jarayonning davomiyligi**:\n   - By next September, he **will have been teaching** for twenty years.\n2. **Kelajakdagi boshqa voqeagacha davom etadigan jarayon**:\n   - By the time you arrive, I **will have been waiting** for two hours.\n3. **Muddat bilan** (for):\n   - She **will have been studying for** six hours by the time the exam starts.\n\n## 3. Future Perfect Continuous vs Future Perfect Simple\n• **Future Perfect Simple** — tugallangan natija muhim.\n  - By Friday, we **will have completed** the project. (tugallangan)\n• **Future Perfect Continuous** — jarayonning davomiyligi muhim.\n  - By Friday, we **will have been working** on the project **for** a month. (qancha vaqt davom etgani muhim)\n\n## 4. Signal so'zlar\n• by, by then, by the time, for + muddat\n• by next week/month/year",
